# ─── KiCad automatic backups ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KiCad writes a copy of the previous save alongside every file. Git already
# does versioning, and these deltas do not compress — they were 92 MB of this
# repo's history before being purged.
*.bak
*-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.sch-bak
*-backups/
_autosave-*
*.000

# ─── Machine-local caches (regenerated by KiCad on open) ────────────────────
# fp-info-cache is a scan of the footprint libraries installed on *your*
# machine. It differs per developer, causes spurious diffs, and was the single
# largest thing in this repo (111 MB across 80 revisions).
fp-info-cache
*.kicad_prl

# KiCad writes the footprint cache to a randomised temp name FIRST and only
# renames it to fp-info-cache on success. An interrupted scan therefore leaves
# a file that `fp-info-cache` above does not match: fp-B625.tmp was tracked in
# CH330N/ for years at 2.5 MB, holding a dump of one developer's local
# footprint libraries. Ignore the temp name too.
fp-*.tmp
*.tmp

# ─── NOT ignored, deliberately ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# *-cache.lib          project-local symbol cache — REQUIRED to open a
#                      schematic on a machine without the original libraries.
# fp-lib-table         project footprint library table.
# sym-lib-table        project symbol library table.
# Do not add these; the designs stop opening cleanly without them.

# ─── Generated manufacturing outputs ────────────────────────────────────────
# Gerbers, drill files and BOMs are built from source and published as
# release assets, not committed.
gerbers/
*.gbr
*.drl
*.gbrjob

# ─── OS / editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
